    $
      F &= 1/(4 pi epsilon_0) dot (Q q)/r^2 \
        &= 8.99 dot 10^9 dot ((1.6 dot 10^(-19))^2)/(1.0 dot 10^(-15))^2 \
        &= 230 "N"
    $

    Same force from both protons, but they have different directions. The difference in
    direction $= 30 degree$.
    \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \

    
    So horizontal components of each vector cancel. So the proton experiences a
    vertical force.
    $
      F &= 2 dot (230 cos (30 degree))
        &= 398.4 N
    $

  + \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
    
    C is equidistant from all protons. This means that at C, the magnitude of each
    individual electric field is the same from al three protons.

    From the vector diagram, we see that if we draw the force vectors that C
    experiences tip to tail, they start and end at the same point.

    This means that the force sums to zero.
    So the resultant electric field strength at C is zero.

